# NeuroChess Autopilot Rules

- Execute at most one queue item per run.
- Use a dedicated worktree for each task unless the task is a local dry run.
- Promotion requires:
  - branch `road-to-V2` up to date before applying changes;
  - no staged files before task execution;
  - changed files inside `allowed_paths`;
  - no files inside `forbidden_paths`;
  - deterministic checks pass;
  - local critic pass or documented degraded mode allowed by policy.
- `docs_tooling` may auto-commit and auto-push to `road-to-V2`.
- `frontend_readonly` may auto-commit and auto-push only with build/typecheck,
  relevant REX smokes, and critic or deterministic visual proof.
- `backend_readonly` may auto-commit and auto-push only with anti-mutation proof.
- `write_sensitive` must quarantine to `autopilot/<task-id>` during bootstrap.
